# @tool jippity-doctor
# @description Diagnose Jippity's local installation, dependencies, desktop support, voice support, and active manifests.
# @command jippity-doctor
# @usage jippity-doctor
# @usage jippity-doctor --json
# @example Why is Jippity voice input not working? Run Jippity Doctor if useful.
# @example Check whether this computer is ready to run Jippity and explain anything I need to fix.
# @installed-by jippity (bundled read-only diagnostic; no network or sandbox bypass needed)
# Run the default report for ordinary troubleshooting; prefer --json for structured inspection.
# Summarize failures and recommended fixes instead of dumping raw JSON. It diagnoses only and never repairs the system.
